From 3f3655f3a6dcf593654c81fb5017d0d735ac7403 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ben Walker <ben@nvidia.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Aug 2024 09:42:35 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 01/17] sock: All sockets must be in groups

Require opts.group when connecting or listening. Accepted sockets
inherit the listener's group. Closing a socket removes it from its
group; explicit remove/add operations remain available to move sockets
between groups.

Provide an internal socket group for NVMe/TCP qpairs that are not in
an NVMe poll group. Preserve the group until deferred socket closure
completes, and report disconnect completion only once the qpair reaches
DISCONNECTED.

Give each ungrouped admin qpair its own socket group so polling one
controller cannot execute another controller's callbacks without its
lock. This avoids global group synchronization at the cost of a socket
group per controller.

Change-Id: I5cd0166e799b2b24f04dffe4cb61eb7587ac5b81
Signed-off-by: Ben Walker <ben@nvidia.com>
